---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import JoinBlock from '../components/JoinBlock.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  path="/about"
  description="Why I'm building open-source infrastructure for composable ontologies — and who this community is for."
>
  <section class="wrap about">
    <h1>Why this exists.</h1>

    <div class="about__body prose-ish">
      <p class="lead">
        Everyone chasing cross-domain intelligence hits the same wall. I hit it
        myself — a real 16,879-node knowledge graph that collapsed under its own
        noise.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The wall is structural: every domain is a unique fingerprint, and one
        schema for all of them destroys what makes each useful. The fix is
        <strong>data-structure infrastructure</strong> — each expert models their
        own domain, then composes. <strong>Open source</strong>: too foundational
        to belong to one vendor.
      </p>

      <div class="about__who bracket">
        <span class="bracket-corners"></span>
        <h3>This is for you if…</h3>
        <ul class="about__list">
          <li>You're building knowledge graphs, entity resolution, or "company brain" tooling and feel the monolith pull.</li>
          <li>You're a domain expert — in medicine, government, ops — who's tired of your team's real model living only in people's heads.</li>
          <li>You just think this way, and want to argue about where the design breaks.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="muted">
        Come find me on <a href={LINKS.xProfile}>X</a>, join the community, or
        sign up for the monthly digest below. No funnel — just the front door.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <hr class="rule" />
    <div style="height:2.5rem"></div>
    <JoinBlock />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem) 1rem;
    max-width: var(--maxw-read);
  }
  .about__body p {
    color: var(--cream-dim);
  }
  .about__who {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    background: var(--bg-panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .about__who h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .about__list {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--cream-dim);
  }
  .about__list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
</style>
